sequenceDiagram
  participant Admin as Enterprise Admin
  participant Broker as Identity Broker
  participant IdP as Enterprise IdP
  participant User as End User
  participant Browser as User Browser

  Note over Admin,Browser: Phase 1: Configuration
  Admin->>Broker: POST /api/v1/tenants (name, slug)
  Broker->>Admin: Tenant ID, API credentials
  Admin->>Broker: POST /tenants/{id}/idp (OIDC config)
  Broker->>Admin: IdP connection established
  Admin->>IdP: Configure broker as authorized app
  Admin->>Broker: POST /tenants/{id}/role-mappings
  Admin->>Broker: Create products & entitlements

  Note over Admin,Browser: Phase 2: SSO Authentication
  User->>Browser: Navigate to application
  Browser->>Broker: Login request
  Broker->>Browser: 302 Redirect to IdP authorization endpoint
  Browser->>IdP: GET /authorize (client_id, redirect_uri, scope)
  IdP->>User: Enterprise login prompt
  User->>IdP: Enter credentials (+ MFA if required)
  IdP->>Browser: 302 Redirect with authorization code

  Note over Admin,Browser: Phase 3: Token Exchange
  Browser->>Broker: GET /auth/callback (code)
  Broker->>IdP: POST /token (exchange code)
  IdP->>Broker: ID Token + Access Token

  Note over Admin,Browser: Phase 4: Tenant Resolution
  Broker->>Broker: Validate ID Token signature (JWKS)
  Broker->>Broker: Extract claims (email, groups, tenant claim)
  Broker->>Broker: Resolve tenant from issuer OR tenant_id claim
  Broker->>Broker: Map external groups to internal roles
  Broker->>Broker: Compute effective entitlements

  Note over Admin,Browser: Phase 5: JWT Issuance
  Broker->>User: Return application JWT
  Note over User: JWT contains:<br/>tenant_id, roles, entitlements
  User->>Browser: Access application with entitlements
